 "result": "When `TESSEL_RUN_FROM_CLI` is `\"true\"`, `Tessel.run` becomes a no-op. The check is at `src/tessel/app.py:695-705`.\n\n- **Not in the reloader:** it prints a red warning, \"Ignoring a call to 'app.run()' that would block the current 'tessel' CLI command. Only call 'app.run()' in an `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` guard.\"\n- **In the reloader process:** it stays silent, so the message doesn't repeat on each reload.\n- **Either way:** it then `return`s before loading dotenv files, applying debug settings or starting the server.\n\nThe variable is set in `TesselGroup.make_context` (`src/tessel/cli.py:667`). The reason is that an unguarded `app.run()` at module level would otherwise start a server on import and block whichever CLI command was being run.",
